>	What are the differences between PC Nethack and the UNIX version?
>I have successfully gotten the amulet and escaped the dungeon without
>ever seeing these items that are frequently mentioned in this newsgroup.
>Am I missing something? (besides a UNIX machine?)
There are very few differences between unix nethack and PC nethack.
The only one I can think of off hand is that there is a mail
daemon in the UNIX version...
>	
>	These are the items:
>
>succubus
A type of demon.  Known for seducing men, #c)hatting with them
can give...umm.... interesting results.
>Unicorn horn
Guess where this one comes from? Very useful, as long as they aren't cursed.
>polymorph traps, polymorph control
Polymorph traps-Traps which cause you to polymorph randomly.  Just like
any other in trap in other respects.  Polymorph control-lets
you control what you poly into.
>giving money to a non-aligned temple priest
Try chatting with the next priest you see.
>altars, temples
Altars-holy places where you can sacrifice monsters.  Temples-
rooms with an altars and a priest(ess)
>drawbridges
Are you *sure* you've beaten nethack without seeing this?  It's the door
to the castle.
>horns, musical instruments, playing music
All musical instruments may be magic or normal.  ALl can be used to open
the castle.
>Medusa
I'm surprised you haven't met Medusa.  Seeing her can be quite a
petrifying experience =)
